  "articleBody": "Deciding when to have a preventive roof inspection can feel a bit like guesswork, but it doesn't have to be. In Texas, where our roofs face everything from intense sun to hail and heavy rains, being proactive is a game-changer. Think of it like getting regular oil changes for your car – it prevents bigger problems. The National Roofing Contractors Association (NRCA) actually suggests you get your roof checked at least twice a year, ideally in spring and fall. These regular inspections help catch small issues before they become major headaches, saving you money and stress in the long run. Knowing the best times to schedule these inspections can really help extend your roof's life and keep your home protected.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\nWhile those bi-annual checks are a great starting point, certain situations definitely call for professional help. If your roof is getting older, or if you've recently experienced severe weather like hail, strong winds, or a major storm, you absolutely need an expert to take a look. Professionals can spot hidden damage, like issues with flashing or subtle hail impacts, that are easy to miss from the ground. Also, if you notice any signs inside your home, like water stains on your ceiling or in your attic, that's a clear signal to call in the pros. Discounted Roofing Co. specializes in these situations, offering detailed inspections and guidance on next steps, especially with insurance claims. Don't wait for a leak to tell you there's a problem; let us help you stay ahead of it.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-03"
}